      "Annakutty Muttathupadathu was born on 19 August 1910 in Kudamalur, Kerala, to a Syro-Malabar Catholic family. Her mother, Maria, died when Annakutty was only a few months old, and she was raised first by her grandparents and later by her aunt. The faith, family prayer and charity she witnessed in childhood shaped her desire to belong completely to God. She received her First Holy Communion in 1917 and attended school while forming friendships beyond her own Christian community.",
      "As she grew older, Annakutty felt drawn to religious life, but relatives hoped she would marry. She resisted repeated efforts to arrange a marriage because she believed she had offered her life to Christ. The Vatican biography records that, in the distress of this struggle, she seriously burned her foot while trying to prevent the marriage plans. The injury left lasting effects and became one of the physical trials that accompanied her life.",
      "With the guidance of her confessor, Father James Muricken, she came into contact with the Franciscan Clarist Congregation. She entered its boarding school at Bharananganam on 24 May 1927, began her postulancy on 2 August 1928 and took the name Alphonsa of the Immaculate Conception. She received the religious habit on 19 May 1930. She taught children at Vakakkad for one school year in 1932 and later served as an assistant teacher, parish catechist and convent secretary whenever her health allowed.",
